  "worked_solution": "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+(-3)y+1z=1 \\\\ 4x+0y+(-1)z=-3 \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+1z=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
